  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Proposal: a members table (workspace, key name, role) checked in the router right after the existing 401 gate",
        "Workspace routes already funnel through one lookup, so the change is one check plus a members section in Workspace settings",
        "guest links are unaffected because they never open a workspace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "Browsers, edge and storage of file bytes, none of which change",
        "Connected but out of scope: cloudflared tunnel, Chunked uploads, Zip streamer, Expiry sweeper, Env file, File bytes on disk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Risks",
      "items": [
        "Every key holder can see, download and delete every workspace: there are no per-workspace permissions; fine for a circle that trusts each other, wrong for mixing groups (see the planned members table)"
      ]
    }
  ]
